title: 'Decide: install-time GPU settings (gpu.amd.integrated, gpu.toolkit) reach
  joined nodes only on re-join, and nothing says so'
updated: 2026-10-31T13:03:35Z
---

Decide (maintainer). From k253 (ocp-worker, 2026-10-31). gpu.amd.integrated (k253) and gpu.toolkit (k223) are install-time settings: they reach a node only when its install task runs. The first control plane gets them on every `ocp apply`. A worker, or police2 and later, gets them only when it is joined again: a Ready node is only verified. Switching integrated true -> false removes nothing (the amdgpu driver stays), and ocp status does not flag a node installed under the other value.

Options:
- (a) Say it: the docs and the apply/status output name the re-join as the way to apply a changed value.
- (b) Record per node, on the OCPNode status, what it was installed with, and have ocp status show it as drift with a manual step.
- (c) Re-run the host step on Ready nodes when the value changes. Disruptive: a driver install, maybe a reboot.

Not to be built before the maintainer answers.
